<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-2751] GridH2TreeIndex.getRowCount unwraps objects&apos; values that are not used later</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2751</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;If to run query like &quot;SELECT COUNT&lt;img class=&quot;emoticon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/emoticons/star_yellow.png&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt; FROM table&quot; then our implementation will perform a full scan filtering out entries that are not primary for a given node and will calculate only a number of primary ones.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If entries are stored off-heap then both a key and value of an entry are unswapped, Unswapped values are not used by backup filters thus we have to omit unswapping of the values at all.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
